<section class="document-page">
<h2>Reporting basis and source notes</h2><p class="sandbox-label"><strong>Sandbox specimen</strong> · Fictional institution and customer data.</p><p class="document-reference">${facts.documentReference} · ${facts.issuedOn}</p>
<dl class="key-details"><div><dt>Entity reference</dt><dd>${facts.resourceReference}</dd></div><div><dt>Reporting basis</dt><dd>Illustrative management basis</dd></div><div><dt>Consolidation scope</dt><dd>Single fictional entity</dd></div><div><dt>Report status</dt><dd>Unaudited sandbox illustration</dd></div></dl><p>For each column, total assets equal total liabilities plus total equity. This fictional report is a specimen of reconciled financial presentation; it is neither an account-balance certificate nor an audited or statutory statement.</p><h2>1. Reporting entity and scope</h2><p>The example covers Single fictional entity. The reporting basis is Illustrative management basis, an illustrative management basis rather than a claim of compliance with an accounting standard. The reporting entity, period, book, currency and consolidation scope must be explicit before a real extract is approved.</p><h2>2. Source mapping and reconciliation</h2><p>Period reference: ${facts.periodReference}. Reconciliation reference: ${facts.reconciliationReference}. The accounting owner must map each included GL/subledger balance to a report line, handle its sign and currency correctly, and prove complete pagination and elimination/adjustment treatment. A balanced presentation alone does not prove source completeness or a closed period.</p><h2>3. Measurement and comparative information</h2><p>Cash, net customer loans, investments, customer deposits and borrowings are fictional amounts. A real report needs approved valuation, impairment, interest, fee, tax and foreign-currency policies, and retains their exact versions. Current and comparative columns each retain separate GL-close and reconciliation snapshot references below. Both use the stated illustrative management basis. A correction needs its own retained approval and lineage.</p><div class="document-legal-note"><strong>Demonstration document.</strong> Firefly Sandbox Financial Services is a fictional demonstration entity. This is an unsigned sandbox specimen with fictional data, not an approved customer form, legal certification, audited report, signature or payment evidence. Approved institution details, source facts, product terms and jurisdiction wording require their own governed revision and authorization.</div>
</section>
